DesOS release identity
=====================

DesOS 0.1 Preview is a private preview distribution built from the Ubuntu 26.04
(Resolute Raccoon) package base and Linux, with the DEs-UI native desktop.
DesOS is a derivative project; Ubuntu, Debian, Linux, dpkg and their components
retain their respective upstream authorship and licenses. This package supplies
DesOS identity metadata, not a replacement for Ubuntu's essential base-files.

Source: image/release_package.py and image/release/ in the DesOS build source.
The build's public JSON record includes archive/payload SHA-256 hashes. No public
download or support service is configured for this private preview.

This package diverts /usr/lib/os-release and /etc/lsb-release to the corresponding
.ubuntu paths before unpacking DesOS metadata. Later base-files updates write
their upstream identity to those diverted paths; DesOS remains the active
identity. /etc/os-release remains base-files' relative symlink into /usr/lib.
Do not edit the .ubuntu backup files to change DesOS branding.

Removal restores the preserved Ubuntu identity. Maintainer scripts refuse a
different package's diversion, another vendor identity, an unclaimed .ubuntu
backup, or a modified active identity during restoration. An administrator must
resolve such a conflict explicitly; the package never discards it automatically.
The release files are package payloads, not conffiles. The normal dpkg remove
step removes them before postrm restores the diverted Ubuntu files.

Maintainer scripts use dpkg's DPKG_ROOT and DPKG_ADMINDIR, allowing the same real
diversion logic to be exercised in a disposable, unprivileged filesystem fixture.
No host package installation is required for those tests.
